  "worked_solution": "Recall Newton's second law, which states that the resultant force $F$ acting on a body equals the product of its mass $m$ and acceleration $a:$\n\n$$\nF=ma\n$$\n\nIn our case, two forces are acting on the wooden box:\n\n- The force due to gravity, given by the weight $w$ of the wooden box, which equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =mg \\\\  & =20g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The force due to drag (air resistance) $D,$ which is proportional to the square of the velocity of the wooden box (and negative since it acts in the negative direction):\n\n$$\nD=-k{v}^{2}=-\\frac{2}{25}{v}^{2}\n$$\n\nSumming the forces, the resultant force acting on the wooden box is\n\n$$\nF=w+D=20g-\\frac{2}{25}{v}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAlso, recall that acceleration is the derivative of velocity: $a=\\frac{dv}{dt}.$\nSubstituting this into Newton's second law, along with our expression for the resultant force on the wooden box, we have\n\n$$\n20g-\\frac{2}{25}{v}^{2}=20\\,\\frac{dv}{dt}\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{dv}{dt}=g-\\frac{1}{250}{v}^{2}.\n$$",
